__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
build/
dist/
deploy/logs/*.log
deploy/.env

# Local secrets. The rule matches the FAMILY, not one filename.
#
# `.env*` rather than `.env` + `.env.*`: the narrower pair misses `.env-backup` and `.envbak`,
# and those are the names a person actually types when setting a config aside. A pattern that
# covers only the name you thought of leaves the next copy exposed — and a secret committed
# once stays in history after any `git rm`.
#
# The negation keeps a versioned template committable — `deploy/.env.example` is one,
# and it is re-included at any depth.
.env*
!.env.example
